    "created_at": "2015-07-13T07:41:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-07-13T07:41:33Z",
    "body": "Do you mean that the new size of an iframe could be observed before the fullscreenchange event is fired? That does seem like a plausible bug if this is implemented as the top-level browsing context exiting fullscreen and notifying its child frames as two separate steps. I don't think it's a fundamental problem though, there's a resize event on window and it ought to be possible to somehow synchronize the fullscreenchange event with that...\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
